  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**02. Acquire Ordinary-Reading Paragraph Reports**\n",
    "\n",
    "Reuse the official ordinary-reading reports or download their two ZIP archives from OSF. Only the Paragraph interest period is required; question, answer and feedback eye movements are outside the input boundary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============== 02. Acquire Ordinary-Reading Paragraph Reports ===============\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------- 1. Acquire or Reuse Original Reports --------------------\n",
    "reports = acquire_reports(raw_dir)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------- 2. Summarise Source Availability ----------------------\n",
    "inventory = pd.DataFrame([{\"report\": k, \"source\": f\"https://osf.io/download/{RESOURCES[k]}/\",\n",
    "                           \"file\": p.name, \"bytes\": p.stat().st_size}\n",
    "                          for k,p in reports.items()])\n",
    "display(inventory)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-03",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**03. Inspect Report Schema and Trial Identity**\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the documented fields. The participant and trial index identify a reading/response trial. Article identifiers are qualified by the article batch; paragraph and question identities preserve that hierarchy. Outcome metadata are used only for cohort selection and scoring."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-03",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =============== 03. Inspect Report Schema and Trial Identity ================\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------------- 1. Load Fixation and Interest-Area Reports -----------------\n",
    "fix = read_report(reports[\"fixations\"], \"fixations\")\n",
    "ia = read_report(reports[\"ia\"], \"ia\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------ 2. Record Report Dimensions ------------------------\n",
    "inventory[\"n_rows\"] = inventory.report.map({\"fixations\":len(fix),\"ia\":len(ia)})\n",
    "inventory[\"n_columns_used\"] = inventory.report.map({\"fixations\":fix.shape[1],\"ia\":ia.shape[1]})\n",
    "display(inventory)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-04",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**04. Reconcile Eligible Reading Trials**\n",
    "\n",
    "Retain first ordinary-reading trials with matched report metadata, a valid A–D answer, a documented correctness label and at least one valid fixation. Exclusion counts describe the union of report trial identities, not the full published corpus."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =================== 04. Reconcile Eligible Reading Trials ===================\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------- 1. Construct the Eligible Cohort ----------------------\n",
    "trials, exclusions = make_cohort(fix, ia)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------------- 2. Summarise Trial and Participant Support -----------------\n",
    "display(exclusions)\n",
    "print(\"Eligible trials:\", len(trials))\n",
    "print(\"Participants:\", trials.participant_id.nunique())\n",
    "print(\"Articles:\", trials.article_key.nunique())\n",
    "del fix, ia\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**05. Define Participant and Article Protocols**\n",
    "\n",
    "Protocol A divides participants within each article batch into approximately 60/20/20 Training, Validation and Test. Protocol B holds out the final article batch and its participants; Training and Validation use separate participants from the other batches. These protocols answer different generalisation questions. Protocol B is a single cross-batch sensitivity analysis, not an external dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-05",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =============== 05. Define Participant and Article Protocols ================\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------ 1. Assign Participant Roles ------------------------\n",
    "splits = make_splits(trials, seed=17)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------- 2. Summarise Outcome Support ------------------------\n",
    "support = (trials.merge(splits,on=\"participant_id\",validate=\"many_to_many\")\n",
    "           .groupby([\"protocol\",\"role\",\"is_correct\"])\n",
    "           .agg(n_trials=(\"trial_id\",\"size\"),n_people=(\"participant_id\",\"nunique\"),\n",
    "                n_articles=(\"article_key\",\"nunique\")).reset_index())\n",
    "display(support)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-06",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**06. Visualise Cohort and Class Support**\n",
    "\n",
    "Inspect trial counts and class balance before modelling. Counts depend on the downloaded reports and eligibility rules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-06",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== 06. Visualise Cohort and Class Support ===================\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------ 1. Plot Participant and Outcome Support ------------------\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(11,4))\n",
    "trials.groupby(\"article_batch\").participant_id.nunique().plot.bar(ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set(xlabel=\"Article batch\",ylabel=\"Participants\",title=\"Eligible cohort\")\n",
    "trials.is_correct.value_counts().sort_index().rename(index={0:\"Incorrect\",1:\"Correct\"}).plot.bar(ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set(xlabel=\"Response\",ylabel=\"Trials\",title=\"Outcome support\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------------- 2. Save Cohort Figure ---------------------------\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "save_figure(fig,out_dir/\"01_cohort_support.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-07",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**07. Save Cohort and Experimental Protocol**\n",
    "\n",
    "Export the current source inventory, exclusion accounting, trial identities, participant assignments and support counts. No raw paragraph text or selected answers are published."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code-07",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================= 07. Save Cohort and Experimental Protocol =================\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------- 1. Save Current Cohort Tables -----------------------\n",
    "for name, frame in {\"01_source_inventory.csv\":inventory,\n",
    "                    \"01_trial_exclusions.csv\":exclusions,\n",
    "                    \"01_trial_index.csv\":trials,\n",
    "                    \"01_participant_splits.csv\":splits,\n",
    "                    \"01_split_support.csv\":support}.items():\n",
    "    frame.to_csv(out_dir/name,index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------ 2. Package Current Outputs -------------------------\n",
    "download_outputs_from_colab(out_dir,\"01\")\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
